      "source": [
        "# Python Variables and Dynamic Typing\n",
        "\n",
        "This notebook demonstrates:\n",
        "1. Creating and printing variables.\n",
        "2. Using variables with formatted strings.\n",
        "3. Adding single-line and multi-line comments.\n",
        "4. Demonstrating dynamic typing in Python."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "c608438c",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 1. Creating and Printing Variables\n",
        "\n",
        "Create three variables named `instaFollowers`, `postLikes`, and `userName`, assign sample values, and print each variable."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "7e2f0004",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Storing Instagram followers, post likes, and username\n",
        "\n",
        "instaFollowers = 1250\n",
        "postLikes = 350\n",
        "userName = \"Prachi\"\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Instagram Followers:\", instaFollowers)\n",
        "print(\"Post Likes:\", postLikes)\n",
        "print(\"Username:\", userName)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "3b179767",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 2. Food Delivery App Variables and Formatted Strings\n",
        "\n",
        "Store the favorite food delivery app's name, the last order amount, and whether a coupon was used. Then print a summary using formatted strings."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "cb71b037",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "\"\"\"\n",
        "This script stores information about my favorite food delivery app,\n",
        "my last order amount, and whether I used a coupon.\n",
        "It then prints the information as a formatted summary.\n",
        "\"\"\"\n",
        "\n",
        "# Name of the favorite food delivery app\n",
        "foodDeliveryApp = \"Zomato\"\n",
        "\n",
        "# Amount paid for the last order\n",
        "lastOrderAmount = 450\n",
        "\n",
        "# Whether a coupon was used for the order\n",
        "usedCoupon = True\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"My favorite food delivery app is {foodDeliveryApp}.\")\n",
        "print(f\"My last order amount was ₹{lastOrderAmount}.\")\n",
        "print(f\"Coupon used: {usedCoupon}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "14295766",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 3. Comments in Python\n",
        "\n",
        "The code above demonstrates both types of comments requested in the assignment:\n",
        "- **Single-line comments:** Written using `#` to explain individual variables or statements.\n",
        "- **Multi-line comments:** Written using triple quotes (`\"\"\"`) to explain the overall purpose of the script."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "982e8b91",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 4. Demonstrating Dynamic Typing\n",
        "\n",
        "Python supports dynamic typing, which means a variable can store a value of one data type and later be reassigned a value of another data type."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "844d505f",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Demonstrating dynamic typing\n",
        "\n",
        "playlistCount = 25\n",
        "print(\"Playlist count:\", playlistCount)\n",
        "\n",
        "playlistCount = \"Twenty-five playlists\"\n",
        "print(\"Playlist count:\", playlistCount)"
      ]
    },
  "nbformat": 4,
  "nbformat_minor": 5
}
